# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# CredCheck environment variables
#
# Nothing here is required to run the app — every feature degrades
# gracefully with zero env vars set: no caching (every scan runs fresh),
# and AI synthesis falls back to the deterministic rule-based scorer.
#
# Copy this file to `.env.local` and fill in what you want to enable.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# --- LLM synthesis (step 8) -------------------------------------------------
# Provider-agnostic. Default is a FREE local model via Ollama, or a
# deterministic rule-based fallback if no LLM is reachable.
#   LLM_PROVIDER=ollama | anthropic | none
LLM_PROVIDER=none
# Ollama (free, local — https://ollama.com). Run: `ollama serve` + `ollama pull llama3.1`
OLLAMA_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434
OLLAMA_MODEL=llama3.1
# Optional paid provider — only used if LLM_PROVIDER=anthropic
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# --- Database / caching ------------------------------------------------------
# Postgres via Prisma. Caches scan results for 48h, and backs /history,
# /report/[id] permalinks, /api/badge, and scam reporting. Optional — without
# it, every scan just runs fresh and those features are disabled (no errors).
#
# Quickest way to get one locally: `npm run db:up` (starts the db service
# defined in docker-compose.yml with matching credentials below), then
# `npm run db:migrate` once to create the tables.
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://credcheck:credcheck@localhost:5432/credcheck?schema=public

# --- Admin moderation queue ---------------------------------------------------
# Gates /admin, where a human approves/rejects crowd-sourced scam reports
# before they count toward scoring. Unset = /admin shows "not configured".
# This is a minimal single-admin password gate, not a full auth system —
# don't reuse a real password here.
# ADMIN_PASSWORD=
